preter for microcontrollers",[403,438,439],{},"ESP32, Raspberry Pi Pico — reduced stdlib.",[374,441,443],{"id":442},"the-gil-one-thread-runs-python-bytecode-at-a-time","The GIL — one thread runs Python bytecode at a time",[19,445,446,447,450,451,454],{},"In the standard CPython build, the ",[30,448,449],{},"Global Interpreter Lock (GIL)"," lets only one thread run Python bytecode at any moment. Threads still help when you wait for I\u002FO (network, disk), because the GIL is released while waiting. They do ",[30,452,453],{},"not"," help for pure-Python math.",[58,456,457],{"language":60},[62,458,460],{"className":64,"code":459,"language":60,"meta":66,"style":66},"import threading, time\n\ndef work():\n    sum(i * i for i in range(5_000_000))\n\nt0 = time.perf_counter()\nwork(); work()\nprint(f\"sequential: {time.perf_counter() - t0:.2f}s\")\n\nt0 = time.perf_counter()\nts = [threading.Thread(target=work) for _ in range(2)]\nfor t in ts: t.start()\nfor t in ts: t.join()\nprint(f\"2 threads:  {time.perf_counter() - t0:.2f}s\")   # about the SAME — not 2× faster\n",[35,461,462,469,473,482,515,519,530,535,571,575,583,618,631,643],{"__ignoreMap":66},[70,463,464,466],{"class":72,"line":73},[70,465,77],{"class":76},[70,467,468],{"class":80}," threading, time\n",[70,470,471],{"class":72,"line":84},[70,472,88],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":87},[70,474,475,477,480],{"class":72,"line":91},[70,476,94],{"class":76},[70,478,479],{"class":97}," work",[70,481,327],{"class":80},[70,483,484,487,490,493,496,499,501,504,507,509,512],{"class":72,"line":104},[70,485,486],{"class":218},"    sum",[70,488,489],{"class":80},"(i ",[70,491,492],{"class":76},"*",[70,494,495],{"class":80}," i ",[70,497,498],{"class":76},"for",[70,500,495],{"class":80},[70,502,503],{"class":76},"in",[70,505,506],{"class":218}," range",[70,508,354],{"class":80},[70,510,511],{"class":218},"5_000_000",[70,513,514],{"class":80},"))\n",[70,516,517],{"class":72,"line":119},[70,518,88],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":87},[70,520,521,